'''Cyclocystoidea''' is a [[class (biology)|class]] of extinct, flattened, more-or-less circular [[echinoderms]] from the [[Ordovician]] to [[Devonian]] periods.  Much about them remains unclear, including their orientation with respect to the substrate, mode of feeding, and general way of life.

==Etymology==

==Description==
Cyclocystoids are circular or slightly oval to sub-pentagonal.

* Central disc (one layer (Smith and Paul) or two?)
* marginal ring of stout perforate ossicles
* encircling peripheral skirt
Notes that rings impreforate ossicles are most likley unusual stromatocystitoids

